

3
00:00:12,554 --> 00:00:15,013
Clean water and breathable air,

4
00:00:15,014 --> 00:00:18,100
the promise of which is a fundamental human right.

5
00:00:18,101 --> 00:00:20,477
EVA Solutions has been keeping that promise alive

6
00:00:20,478 --> 00:00:24,564
for over a decade since
founder Desmond Frey's unveiling

7
00:00:24,565 --> 00:00:29,486
of the very first EVA prototype
to the EVA units used today.

8
00:00:29,487 --> 00:00:33,950
A drop of hope in a world of desperation. EVA.

9
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:40,623
Lights on.

10
00:00:41,624 --> 00:00:46,337
Ambient temperature, 23 degrees Celsius. AQI, 151.

11
00:00:47,255 --> 00:00:50,173
Laura.

12
00:00:50,174 --> 00:00:51,051
Laura.

13
00:00:55,763 --> 00:00:57,180
There she is.

14
00:00:57,181 --> 00:00:58,933
How'd you sleep?

15
00:01:00,852 --> 00:01:03,478
Good. You? - Good.

16
00:01:03,479 --> 00:01:04,355
Good.

17
00:01:12,072 --> 00:01:14,781
Gotta stay inside today. Index is 150.

18
00:01:14,782 --> 00:01:15,741
Dad, please.

19
00:01:15,742 --> 00:01:18,493
Air quality index over 125, I gotta ground you.

20
00:01:18,494 --> 00:01:19,370
You know that.

21
00:01:20,246 --> 00:01:21,329
Am I getting worse?

22
00:01:21,330 --> 00:01:22,706
No.

23
00:01:22,707 --> 00:01:27,712
No, it's just precautionary. Hey, chin up.

24
00:01:28,838 --> 00:01:30,547
We could work on one of our projects today.

25
00:01:30,548 --> 00:01:31,423
You got the part?

26
00:01:31,424 --> 00:01:34,468
Not exactly, but there has been a plan

27
00:01:34,469 --> 00:01:35,719
that's been put into motion.

28
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:38,597
I think I found a way into his compound.

29
00:01:38,598 --> 00:01:39,891
Just need a little time.

30
00:01:42,852 --> 00:01:46,563
These guys think they own
everything. The air, the water.

31
00:01:46,564 --> 00:01:47,774
What's next?

32
00:01:54,364 --> 00:01:56,990
Let's keep you on extra water until you improve.

33
00:01:56,991 --> 00:01:58,408
What about yours?

34
00:01:58,409 --> 00:01:59,828
I'll be fine this morning.

35
00:02:17,178 --> 00:02:18,179
Inhale.

36
00:02:20,932 --> 00:02:24,477
Exhale. Warrior two.

37
00:02:28,148 --> 00:02:30,525
Inhale. Hold.

38
00:02:31,693 --> 00:02:33,987
Exhale. Lower down.

39
00:02:36,948 --> 00:02:38,908
Inhale. Pull through.

40
00:02:42,495 --> 00:02:44,414
Press back. Down dog.

41
00:02:48,418 --> 00:02:50,920
Inhale. Rise.

42
00:02:57,218 --> 00:02:59,262
Exhale. Fold.

43
00:03:04,184 --> 00:03:06,102
Step right foot forward.

44
00:03:08,646 --> 00:03:10,313
Inhale.

45
00:03:10,314 --> 00:03:13,860
Rise. Warrior two.

46
00:03:14,694 --> 00:03:15,986
Find focus.

47
00:03:15,987 --> 00:03:16,863
End sequence.

48
00:03:18,656 --> 00:03:20,325
Namaste, Desmond.

49
00:03:30,251 --> 00:03:31,042
And more about

50
00:03:31,043 --> 00:03:32,127
the situation here.

51
00:03:32,128 --> 00:03:35,088
First, let's go live to Emma Evans in the field.

52
00:03:35,089 --> 00:03:35,964
Hi, Genevieve.

53
00:03:35,965 --> 00:03:38,216
I'm here on location in downtown Los Angeles

54
00:03:38,217 --> 00:03:40,886
where protesters are angry about the failed vote

55
00:03:40,887 --> 00:03:42,387
to... Hey.

56
00:03:42,388 --> 00:03:44,933
It's a little too early for that, don't you think?

57
00:03:46,059 --> 00:03:48,269
We're supposed to be saving water, remember?

58
00:03:52,106 --> 00:03:53,398
Okay.

59
00:03:53,399 --> 00:03:56,193
This is filter compound test number 107.

60
00:03:56,194 --> 00:03:58,945
Beginning water purification test.

61
00:03:58,946 --> 00:04:01,615
Primer ready. Starting synthesis.

62
00:04:01,616 --> 00:04:03,450
Toxicity level dropping.

63
00:04:03,451 --> 00:04:04,827
Toxins parts per million?

64
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:07,996
20,000 and dropping.

65
00:04:07,997 --> 00:04:09,623
Energy's neutralising.

66
00:04:09,624 --> 00:04:12,959
Keep an eye on radiation levels before the PPM drops.

67
00:04:12,960 --> 00:04:14,002
Let me know when.

68
00:04:14,003 --> 00:04:15,629
Now.

69
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:17,090
PPM at 10,000...

70
00:04:18,967 --> 00:04:20,300
Filter failure.

71
00:04:20,301 --> 00:04:24,179
Water toxicity above safe consumption threshold.

72
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:25,056
It's okay.

73
00:04:27,433 --> 00:04:30,812
There's still the EVA beta.

74
00:04:43,616 --> 00:04:46,785
The FOV was on the fritz, so I had to reset it.

75
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:48,246
Seems like it's working now.

76
00:04:49,747 --> 00:04:52,666
No substitute for the whole thing, I guess, though, huh?

77
00:04:52,667 --> 00:04:54,294
I'll put in a service request.

78
00:05:05,346 --> 00:05:10,351
So, you meeting with the board today?

79
00:05:12,353 --> 00:05:13,229
Board?

80
00:05:14,314 --> 00:05:16,731
You mean the guys who I
made rich over the last 10 years

81
00:05:16,732 --> 00:05:18,860
and now they want to push me out of my own company?

82
00:05:20,528 --> 00:05:23,655
No matter what, you know I support you, right?

83
00:05:23,656 --> 00:05:25,949
You've worked so hard to build all of this.

84
00:05:25,950 --> 00:05:28,493
You did that, for us.

85
00:05:28,494 --> 00:05:33,541
And it's great and I love it, but we don't need any of this.

86
00:05:36,336 --> 00:05:37,337
I'm good either way.

87
00:05:39,213 --> 00:05:40,048
I know.

88
00:05:42,467 --> 00:05:44,050
Okay, well, anyways,

89
00:05:44,051 --> 00:05:46,886
I'm gonna head out for a bit, so I'll see you later, yeah?

90
00:05:46,887 --> 00:05:48,639
Yeah. See you later. - Good.

91
00:05:52,769 --> 00:05:53,727
Why don't you come with me?

92
00:05:53,728 --> 00:05:55,813
You know, get out of this fortress.

93
00:05:57,190 --> 00:05:58,775
The real world does still exist.

94
00:06:01,611 --> 00:06:02,820
Maybe next time, okay?

95
00:06:16,042 --> 00:06:17,751
The position isn't so cut and dry.

96
00:06:17,752 --> 00:06:22,339
However, Mr. Frey is a visionary, a genius, if you will.

97
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:24,341
But to fix these issues takes strategy,

98
00:06:24,342 --> 00:06:26,843
rationing, implementing laws, and so on.

99
00:06:26,844 --> 00:06:29,346
Shareholders are getting
weary of the constant bad news.

100
00:06:29,347 --> 00:06:31,933
That's not good for EVA or anyone else.

101
00:06:33,684 --> 00:06:35,310
New residents losing hope

102
00:06:35,311 --> 00:06:40,190
that as development slows
and land ownership appeals...

103
00:06:40,191 --> 00:06:43,276
Who claim that EVA is selling water

104
00:06:43,277 --> 00:06:46,404
to the highest bidder.

105
00:06:46,405 --> 00:06:47,365
You okay?

106
00:06:48,533 --> 00:06:49,741
If you're thirsty, we could get some water

107
00:06:49,742 --> 00:06:51,993
from rations, just for today.

108
00:06:51,994 --> 00:06:55,289
No thanks, Dad. I'll be fine for today.

109
00:06:57,166 --> 00:06:59,876
I have their best interests at-

110
00:06:59,877 --> 00:07:02,338
Clean water is a basic human right.

111
00:07:03,881 --> 00:07:06,384
Would you plan to make this available to everyone?

112
00:07:09,804 --> 00:07:11,264
I'm gonna go take a shower.

113
00:07:12,974 --> 00:07:14,308
Why don't you get ready for bed?

114
00:07:15,685 --> 00:07:17,270
It's a simple question.

115
00:07:19,105 --> 00:07:21,399
Mr. Frank? I mean, ballpark.

116
00:07:24,735 --> 00:07:26,863
Sonic chamber initialising.

117
00:07:54,098 --> 00:07:55,723
Breaking news.

118
00:07:55,724 --> 00:07:58,643
In a sudden move, EVA Solutions founder and CEO,

119
00:07:58,644 --> 00:08:01,020
Desmond Frey, met with board members today

120
00:08:01,021 --> 00:08:02,814
and announced intentions to leave the company

121
00:08:02,815 --> 00:08:04,983
and relinquish his controlling
shares to the next owner.

122
00:08:04,984 --> 00:08:07,152
No... - Emma.

123
00:08:07,153 --> 00:08:09,821
Genevieve, while this is a new development,

124
00:08:09,822 --> 00:08:12,449
the questions and concerns
regarding the source code

125
00:08:12,450 --> 00:08:13,283
for the EVA-

126
00:08:13,284 --> 00:08:15,118
Dad? - Technology remain.

127
00:08:15,119 --> 00:08:16,077
What is known

128
00:08:16,078 --> 00:08:19,414
is that Mr. Frey will be leaving EVA Solutions.

129
00:08:19,415 --> 00:08:21,749
Many expect shareholder
fallout from creating room

130
00:08:21,750 --> 00:08:23,628
for the new leadership to craft a future...

131
00:08:27,715 --> 00:08:30,051
Good night, Angel, I love you.

132
00:08:58,871 --> 00:09:00,540
Good night, Mr. Frey.

133
00:09:19,183 --> 00:09:23,271
Good morning, Desmond. Starting morning sequence.

134
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:11,317
Visitor. Front door.

135
00:10:11,318 --> 00:10:14,322
Maintenance tech alpha, 1756.

136
00:10:16,657 --> 00:10:18,575
Visitor. Front door.

137
00:10:18,576 --> 00:10:21,160
Maintenance tech alpha, 1756.

138
00:10:29,086 --> 00:10:30,463
He's here to fix the FOV.

139
00:10:31,589 --> 00:10:32,755
I never sent a request.

140
00:10:32,756 --> 00:10:34,467
Oh, it was an automatic request.

141
00:10:35,635 --> 00:10:37,385
Well, you got it?

142
00:10:37,386 --> 00:10:38,553
I'll be upstairs.

143
00:10:38,554 --> 00:10:40,096
I'm alpha one... No.

144
00:10:40,097 --> 00:10:44,142
Alpha 1756, I'm sorry.

145
00:10:44,143 --> 00:10:45,019
That was rude.

146
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:48,563
I'm Desmond.

147
00:10:48,564 --> 00:10:50,273
No problem. I'm George.

148
00:10:50,274 --> 00:10:52,276
Incoming call. Urgent.

149
00:10:53,319 --> 00:10:54,402
George, I have to take this.

150
00:10:54,403 --> 00:10:56,195
Can you find your way there?

151
00:10:56,196 --> 00:10:57,655
The panel is over there by the FOV.

152
00:10:57,656 --> 00:11:00,660
Incoming call. Urgent. - Yes, sir.

153
00:11:31,065 --> 00:11:32,649
You all done?

154
00:11:32,650 --> 00:11:35,236
Uh, yeah.

155
00:11:36,195 --> 00:11:37,528
Let's grab a drink.

156
00:11:37,529 --> 00:11:40,698
Oh, I don't drink.

157
00:11:40,699 --> 00:11:41,575
I insist.

158
00:11:55,089 --> 00:11:58,841
You like the view? I had other options, you know.

159
00:11:58,842 --> 00:12:02,845
Martian colonies, the floating
cities in the clean zone.

160
00:12:02,846 --> 00:12:05,139
But I chose this place.

161
00:12:05,140 --> 00:12:07,058
I guess something about it reminds me of the part

162
00:12:07,059 --> 00:12:10,687
of my life that once was.

163
00:12:10,688 --> 00:12:12,440
Of course it all looks different now.

164
00:12:14,734 --> 00:12:15,568
Of course.

165
00:12:17,737 --> 00:12:20,196
You wanna know how I got to where I am?

166
00:12:20,197 --> 00:12:23,075
It was George, right? Know how I got where I am, George?

167
00:12:24,910 --> 00:12:29,749
Eight years ago, I designed the first EVA device.

168
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:33,084
The EVA beta.

169
00:12:33,085 --> 00:12:35,002
It was the first working
prototype that would lead us

170
00:12:35,003 --> 00:12:37,046
to the EVA pure units today.

171
00:12:37,047 --> 00:12:40,258
I keep it here where I can see it every day to remind me.

172
00:12:40,259 --> 00:12:42,468
You have any idea what it takes to start a company?

173
00:12:42,469 --> 00:12:44,054
The magnitude of sacrifice?

174
00:12:45,055 --> 00:12:45,847
It's amazing.

175
00:12:45,848 --> 00:12:50,895
You should be very proud. Thanks for the water.

176
00:12:52,104 --> 00:12:57,109
But I really should be going. But yeah, it's...

177
00:12:57,318 --> 00:12:58,152
Beautiful?

178
00:12:59,987 --> 00:13:04,074
Yes, it is. This construction is impeccable.

179
00:13:05,242 --> 00:13:06,911
Honestly, the design is flawless.

180
00:13:08,329 --> 00:13:11,207
It's a wonderfully tooled replica.

181
00:13:16,045 --> 00:13:17,920
It's incredible, but something like this just

182
00:13:17,921 --> 00:13:20,466
has a soul that can't be replicated.

183
00:13:21,467 --> 00:13:26,472
I knew the second I saw it.
Security is already on its way.

184
00:13:28,057 --> 00:13:30,308
I'm assuming mine's in the bag there.

185
00:13:30,309 --> 00:13:33,187
Why don't we go ahead and
put that back where it belongs?

186
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:35,605
Though I got to ask you,

187
00:13:35,606 --> 00:13:38,025
why steal something that only has meaning to me?

188
00:13:39,568 --> 00:13:43,029
You have no idea what this represents. The work.

189
00:13:43,030 --> 00:13:44,947
The ingenuity it took to create.

190
00:13:44,948 --> 00:13:47,992
You see, that's the difference between you and me.

191
00:13:47,993 --> 00:13:49,370
That's why I am where I am.

192
00:14:11,475 --> 00:14:12,767
No.

193
00:14:12,768 --> 00:14:14,227
No?

194
00:14:14,228 --> 00:14:16,438
This is the difference between you and I.

195
00:14:17,314 --> 00:14:20,734
For you it's all about money and profit. But to us?

196
00:14:24,488 --> 00:14:27,491
It's about life and death. And sacrifice?

197
00:14:28,617 --> 00:14:31,828
You can talk to me about sacrifice?

198
00:14:31,829 --> 00:14:33,831
Have you ever had to ration your water?

199
00:14:35,457 --> 00:14:38,459
Water that if you drank it would just make you sick?

200
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:41,212
You'd die from dehydration if you didn't?

201
00:14:41,213 --> 00:14:44,549
Yeah, if we had one of your EV units we'd be fine.

202
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:45,843
But no one can afford it.

203
00:14:46,719 --> 00:14:49,262
They don't even have them in our quadrants.

204
00:14:49,263 --> 00:14:52,682
And even if they did we'd
have to keep getting new filters.

205
00:14:52,683 --> 00:14:55,269
It's a never-ending uphill battle.

206
00:14:57,646 --> 00:14:58,689
I don't understand.

207
00:14:59,815 --> 00:15:01,941
What did you come here for today?

208
00:15:01,942 --> 00:15:02,900
I don't have the technology

209
00:15:02,901 --> 00:15:05,403
to reverse engineer the new units.

210
00:15:05,404 --> 00:15:07,113
So I needed the source code from the original.

211
00:15:07,114 --> 00:15:08,573
Reverse engineer?

212
00:15:08,574 --> 00:15:10,867
Do you have any idea how complex the design is?

213
00:15:10,868 --> 00:15:12,952
I figured most of it out, Desmond.

214
00:15:12,953 --> 00:15:14,538
It's photocatalytic elements.

215
00:15:16,582 --> 00:15:18,082
I just can't figure it out how you protected

216
00:15:18,083 --> 00:15:20,084
the plasma-facing elements in the edge region

217
00:15:20,085 --> 00:15:21,629
while powering the synthesis.

218
00:15:22,713 --> 00:15:27,718
That's why I needed the source code. That's why I'm here.

219
00:15:35,225 --> 00:15:36,267
You know when I started this company

220
00:15:36,268 --> 00:15:37,603
it wasn't about the money.

221
00:15:40,314 --> 00:15:42,315
But there are so many things
that stand in the way, George.

222
00:15:42,316 --> 00:15:43,359
You have no idea.

223
00:15:49,365 --> 00:15:51,450
This wasn't my intention. Any of this.

224
00:15:58,290 --> 00:16:00,416
I have a daughter.

225
00:16:00,417 --> 00:16:05,005
She's not well. This was my only option.

226
00:16:09,885 --> 00:16:11,428
Take it. - Excuse me?

227
00:16:12,763 --> 00:16:14,221
The EVA beta.

228
00:16:14,222 --> 00:16:18,727
Take it. I had a daughter too.

229
00:16:19,895 --> 00:16:20,729
A long time ago.

230
00:16:23,524 --> 00:16:25,275
I admire your tenacity.

231
00:16:27,486 --> 00:16:29,822
Go ahead. Security won't stop you.

232
00:16:38,622 --> 00:16:41,291
What was your daughter's name?

233
00:16:42,584 --> 00:16:43,419
Eva.

234
00:16:57,975 --> 00:16:59,684
FOV, deactivate.

235
00:16:59,685 --> 00:17:01,562
Field of view shutting down.

236
00:17:44,271 --> 00:17:45,939
Look what I found.

237
00:17:51,278 --> 00:17:55,282
I told you not to eat like that. Fuel, not food.

238
00:17:59,536 --> 00:18:00,370
Better.

239
00:18:04,458 --> 00:18:05,501
We have to get going.

240
00:18:31,068 --> 00:18:33,028
You stand a better chance without me.

241
00:18:34,696 --> 00:18:36,073
We're doing this together.

242
00:18:41,870 --> 00:18:43,913
Do you trust this claim or not?

243
00:18:43,914 --> 00:18:45,916
I don't really have a choice.

244
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:48,751
I thought you lot were supposed

245
00:18:48,752 --> 00:18:50,170
to have the answer to everything.

246
00:18:51,421 --> 00:18:53,006
I'm not flying, remember?

247
00:18:54,967 --> 00:18:55,801
Don't smile.

248
00:18:56,677 --> 00:18:57,511
It's human.

249
00:19:01,974 --> 00:19:02,808
Better.

250
00:19:15,696 --> 00:19:20,200
I told you. You can't afford to be tired or hurting.

251
00:19:26,832 --> 00:19:27,998
Is there a way of teaching me these things

252
00:19:27,999 --> 00:19:29,001
without hurting me?

253
00:19:31,879 --> 00:19:33,129
It's not personal.

254
00:19:33,130 --> 00:19:35,089
I've shown you how to shut down your mental

255
00:19:35,090 --> 00:19:36,592
and physical impulses.

256
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:39,678
Cosmetics alone won't get you in.

257
00:19:44,766 --> 00:19:45,976
Soften your expression.

258
00:19:49,146 --> 00:19:50,354
Better.

259
00:19:50,355 --> 00:19:52,482
We're not all built anatomically perfect

260
00:19:53,358 --> 00:19:56,278
like you.

261
00:20:14,588 --> 00:20:16,380
Shall we give them some food?

262
00:20:16,381 --> 00:20:17,257
Come.

263
00:20:24,514 --> 00:20:27,474
It's healthy. What are you doing?

264
00:20:27,475 --> 00:20:29,353
Spots. - Not for you?

265
00:20:33,982 --> 00:20:34,982
Get in. - What are you doing?!

266
00:20:34,983 --> 00:20:37,610
Get in!

267
00:20:37,611 --> 00:20:38,652
Hey! - Hey!

268
00:20:38,653 --> 00:20:39,945
What are they doing! - Hey!

269
00:20:39,946 --> 00:20:41,864
Get out of our car!

270
00:20:41,865 --> 00:20:43,782
Hey! What are they doing!

271
00:20:43,783 --> 00:20:46,660
What are you doing?

272
00:20:46,661 --> 00:20:51,582
Drive!

273
00:21:08,892 --> 00:21:11,812
I can't believe it. Are you okay?

274
00:21:18,318 --> 00:21:20,779
Your face is betraying your thoughts.

275
00:21:25,158 --> 00:21:26,410
We took their home.

276
00:21:28,578 --> 00:21:31,080
This is not a home, it's a vehicle.

277
00:21:31,081 --> 00:21:32,624
They can make another shelter.

278
00:21:35,836 --> 00:21:37,629
I know you feel emotion.

279
00:21:41,216 --> 00:21:43,218
Feeling and showing is not the same.

280
00:23:30,575 --> 00:23:31,742
I thought this place was supposed to be overflowing

281
00:23:31,743 --> 00:23:32,619
with people.

282
00:23:34,454 --> 00:23:36,581
Some died, some returned.

283
00:23:38,708 --> 00:23:39,668
Only some get in.

284
00:24:39,186 --> 00:24:40,729
Can you still help my sister?

285
00:24:43,148 --> 00:24:44,816
You're gonna need a lot of work.

286
00:25:06,171 --> 00:25:08,757
Here, can you stir that for me?

287
00:25:18,808 --> 00:25:20,644
Why did you learn all this?

288
00:25:22,938 --> 00:25:25,063
Even when you were through,

289
00:25:25,064 --> 00:25:27,400
any sign of emotion will ground you a radical.

290
00:25:29,236 --> 00:25:30,654
You're there on their terms.

291
00:25:32,697 --> 00:25:35,951
Once denied, they will never let you in.

292
00:25:37,285 --> 00:25:38,327
What else do I need to know?

293
00:25:38,328 --> 00:25:40,121
You do not need to know anything.

294
00:25:41,081 --> 00:25:42,289
Knowledge is not necessary.

295
00:25:42,290 --> 00:25:43,999
Humanity is not necessary.

296
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:46,919
Humanity is back there killing themselves.

297
00:25:46,920 --> 00:25:51,925
That is why you must take the girl, as promised.

298
00:25:52,175 --> 00:25:55,178
When we have our status, we will come back for her.

299
00:25:59,099 --> 00:26:00,100
I'm trusting you.

300
00:26:03,478 --> 00:26:04,688
We'll be back for her.

301
00:26:09,901 --> 00:26:11,945
This is going to be cold.

302
00:27:40,450 --> 00:27:41,284
Forward.

303
00:28:01,304 --> 00:28:02,138
Forward.

304
00:28:15,151 --> 00:28:17,402
Go through. - Can I wait?

305
00:28:17,403 --> 00:28:18,530
Go through.

306
00:28:40,510 --> 00:28:41,344
Forward.

307
00:29:38,151 --> 00:29:40,153
We'll be back for her.

308
00:29:44,783 --> 00:29:46,201
Memories are like dreams.

309
00:29:47,410 --> 00:29:50,830
They take us far away, to moments lost in time.

310
00:29:53,500 --> 00:29:55,543
They're imperfect, just like us.

311
00:29:57,712 --> 00:30:00,340
But my memories are nightmares I can't unsee.

312
00:30:01,883 --> 00:30:04,552
In the darkness of my mind my mother lives on.

313
00:30:05,720 --> 00:30:08,306
But so does the monster that took her away from me.

314
00:30:10,725 --> 00:30:11,559
Mommy...

315
00:30:17,273 --> 00:30:19,067
Then I will find him.

316
00:31:44,819 --> 00:31:46,821
You shouldn't be here.

317
00:32:10,970 --> 00:32:12,472
Are you alright?

318
00:32:14,015 --> 00:32:18,144
Hey, look at me. You're gonna be fine.

319
00:32:28,029 --> 00:32:29,280
Find a way out.

320
00:32:42,377 --> 00:32:44,629
This place is a mess.

321
00:32:56,140 --> 00:32:57,016
He's watching us.

322
00:33:09,821 --> 00:33:13,073
Halt.

323
00:33:13,074 --> 00:33:13,950
Collins.

324
00:33:22,291 --> 00:33:24,626
We have to get out of here before it's too late.

325
00:33:24,627 --> 00:33:25,962
It's only gonna get worse.

326
00:33:27,630 --> 00:33:28,464
Johnson?

327
00:33:29,382 --> 00:33:30,299
How do you know?

328
00:33:34,303 --> 00:33:35,471
I've been here before.

329
00:33:41,853 --> 00:33:45,897
Pay attention.

330
00:34:33,196 --> 00:34:34,030
Mommy.

331
00:35:22,203 --> 00:35:23,037
Daddy?

332
00:35:30,503 --> 00:35:31,337
Lauren.

333
00:35:32,588 --> 00:35:33,422
Baby.

334
00:35:49,981 --> 00:35:52,066
It was never you fault.

335
00:36:15,006 --> 00:36:16,507
Are you alright?

336
00:36:34,275 --> 00:36:35,109
Lauren?

337
00:36:40,781 --> 00:36:41,616
Lauren?

338
00:37:00,635 --> 00:37:02,970
We can't change our past.

339
00:37:03,930 --> 00:37:08,433
We can remember, forget, move on.

340
00:37:08,434 --> 00:37:13,062
How are you feeling? - Dreams, nightmares.

341
00:37:13,063 --> 00:37:17,401
They all end the same way. We just need to open our eyes.

342
00:37:20,112 --> 00:37:24,450
And after all this time, I'm finally awake.

343
00:39:27,448 --> 00:39:30,533
Laura.

344
00:39:30,534 --> 00:39:32,910
Hebrah? Is it you?

345
00:39:32,911 --> 00:39:33,788
Yes.

346
00:39:41,462 --> 00:39:42,880
We were told...

347
00:39:44,590 --> 00:39:46,674
We thought we lost you.

348
00:39:46,675 --> 00:39:49,136
How is Naira? - Holding on.

349
00:39:50,346 --> 00:39:52,305
She misses you so very dearly.

350
00:39:52,306 --> 00:39:54,265
We'll all be over soon.

351
00:39:54,266 --> 00:39:56,893
I've spoken to the others.

352
00:39:56,894 --> 00:39:58,853
We are close to making a push.

353
00:39:58,854 --> 00:40:00,398
Just tell me when and where.

354
00:40:01,440 --> 00:40:02,274
We'll be ready.

355
00:40:05,111 --> 00:40:07,362
Look for the lights in the sky.

356
00:40:07,363 --> 00:40:09,573
Come to the spot with her.

357
00:42:49,650 --> 00:42:54,654
5718. Surrender yourself.

358
00:43:52,421 --> 00:43:53,255
Hello?

359
00:43:54,423 --> 00:43:57,758
Hebrah? - Are you at the location?

360
00:43:57,759 --> 00:43:59,218
Yes.

361
00:43:59,219 --> 00:44:00,679
Yes, we are here.

362
00:44:22,534 --> 00:44:26,288
No!

363
00:44:46,850 --> 00:44:47,685
Wait.

364
00:46:24,740 --> 00:46:27,910
Do you think the others made it out?

365
00:46:49,348 --> 00:46:51,849
Breaking down the wall was just the start.

366
00:46:51,850 --> 00:46:55,770
For so long, hybrids like me
were torn from our parents

367
00:46:55,771 --> 00:46:59,023
and had to hide because people were scared of us.

368
00:46:59,024 --> 00:47:00,859
Now, I'm back with my family.

369
00:47:01,693 --> 00:47:04,695
And I wish everyone would one day see that love

370
00:47:04,696 --> 00:47:06,824
is stronger than fear.

371
00:47:13,956 --> 00:47:17,082
Hi, mom. It's been a while.

372
00:47:17,083 --> 00:47:21,295
We've been touring village after village, as usual.

373
00:47:21,296 --> 00:47:24,131
Yesterday we got called in to help out at a village

374
00:47:24,132 --> 00:47:27,301
that was under heavy fire.

375
00:47:27,302 --> 00:47:29,887
We helped get these kids out of a school.

376
00:47:29,888 --> 00:47:33,725
And then when we reunited them with their families,

377
00:47:35,477 --> 00:47:37,187
it started snowing.

378
00:47:38,105 --> 00:47:41,316
It never snows here. It reminded me of home.

379
00:47:42,276 --> 00:47:44,361
And of you and dad.

380
00:47:49,575 --> 00:47:52,202
I just wanted to let you know I was thinking of you.

381
00:47:53,620 --> 00:47:54,913
I love you, mom. Bye.

382
00:47:56,373 --> 00:47:58,458
I love you, mom. Bye.

383
00:47:59,918 --> 00:48:01,044
I love you, mom...

384
00:48:13,807 --> 00:48:15,309
Okay. Let's see.

385
00:48:23,984 --> 00:48:26,028
Wow.

386
00:48:34,494 --> 00:48:35,329
Hi.

387
00:48:37,039 --> 00:48:37,873
Hello.

388
00:48:38,916 --> 00:48:40,125
I am Sheila.

389
00:48:40,959 --> 00:48:43,669
Shilah. - Sheila.

390
00:48:43,670 --> 00:48:46,130
Shilah. - Better.

391
00:48:46,131 --> 00:48:49,426
It'll come. It's very nice to meet you.

392
00:48:52,179 --> 00:48:54,889
Fist bump? High five?

393
00:48:54,890 --> 00:48:56,599
Oh.

394
00:48:56,600 --> 00:48:58,225
Cool.

395
00:48:58,226 --> 00:49:00,853
I am... - Oh, Melo.

396
00:49:00,854 --> 00:49:04,148
I know. It's a lovely name.

397
00:49:04,149 --> 00:49:07,192
All right, then. There's a lot that I have to show you.

398
00:49:07,193 --> 00:49:09,863
Follow me.

399
00:49:48,402 --> 00:49:50,028
Sheila.

400
00:49:51,196 --> 00:49:52,906
You're the smartest girl I know.

401
00:49:54,908 --> 00:49:57,369
Yeah. Both you and your daddy.

402
00:49:58,662 --> 00:50:00,537
I can help you blow these out. Ready?

403
00:50:00,538 --> 00:50:03,917
One, two, three.

404
00:50:08,338 --> 00:50:09,755
I know.

405
00:50:09,756 --> 00:50:13,801
I love you too, honey. Eight.

406
00:50:13,802 --> 00:50:14,635
Sheila. - How did you

407
00:50:14,636 --> 00:50:15,887
get to be so big.

408
00:50:17,305 --> 00:50:19,099
Your hair is so soft.

409
00:50:25,230 --> 00:50:26,273
This is great.

410
00:50:30,318 --> 00:50:33,405
Oh my gosh. Melo, what are you doing?

411
00:50:34,531 --> 00:50:36,366
Is dinner ready? Okay.

412
00:50:37,242 --> 00:50:38,243
I'll be right there.

413
00:50:40,370 --> 00:50:45,292
♪ I never planned falling in love with you ♪

414
00:50:51,423 --> 00:50:53,590
♪ I never planned falling ♪

415
00:50:53,591 --> 00:50:55,509
That's so sweet of you,

416
00:50:55,510 --> 00:50:57,845
but I need this glass for drinking.

417
00:50:57,846 --> 00:50:59,013
Oh.

418
00:50:59,014 --> 00:51:01,432
Oh, don't look so sad, silly.

419
00:51:01,433 --> 00:51:02,975
It's okay.

420
00:51:02,976 --> 00:51:06,603
♪ Always thought forever ♪

421
00:51:06,604 --> 00:51:11,651
♪ I wanted to ♪

422
00:51:12,903 --> 00:51:15,696
♪ This wonderful life of mine ♪

423
00:51:15,697 --> 00:51:16,907
That's snow.

424
00:51:17,824 --> 00:51:18,658
Wow.

425
00:51:19,534 --> 00:51:21,535
My daughter, she loves snow more

426
00:51:21,536 --> 00:51:24,121
than anything else.

427
00:51:24,122 --> 00:51:27,751
♪ And knowing the storm... ♪

428
00:51:32,005 --> 00:51:36,133
Speaking of my daughter, you, my new friend,

429
00:51:36,134 --> 00:51:38,095
are in for a real treat.

430
00:51:44,768 --> 00:51:45,644
Do you like it?

431
00:51:47,020 --> 00:51:47,854
Yeah.

432
00:51:49,231 --> 00:51:51,482
My daughter and my husband,

433
00:51:51,483 --> 00:51:54,986
they used to sit together at
that piano for hours every day.

434
00:51:57,739 --> 00:51:59,116
Could you teach me?

435
00:52:01,785 --> 00:52:02,619
Why not?

436
00:52:04,246 --> 00:52:06,373
We're going to begin with scales.

437
00:52:11,336 --> 00:52:12,337
Ah, uh, hmm.

438
00:52:16,633 --> 00:52:17,966
Okay.

439
00:52:17,967 --> 00:52:19,676
So one finger at a time.

440
00:52:19,677 --> 00:52:20,511
Okay.

441
00:52:20,512 --> 00:52:22,096
Start with your thumb on C.

442
00:52:22,097 --> 00:52:24,932
Right there. And it looks and sounds like this.

443
00:52:30,939 --> 00:52:35,067
My husband learned this faster than you are. It's okay.

444
00:52:35,068 --> 00:52:36,527
It's all right. Try again.

445
00:52:36,528 --> 00:52:38,612
Come on. We'll do it together.

446
00:52:38,613 --> 00:52:40,740
Thumb on C. Ready?

447
00:52:48,582 --> 00:52:50,041
Keep practising. Okay?

448
00:52:51,293 --> 00:52:54,462
Mm-hmm.

449
00:53:12,147 --> 00:53:14,357
Come on, come on, come on.

450
00:53:22,908 --> 00:53:23,742
Hmm...

451
00:55:36,041 --> 00:55:36,875
Mm...

452
00:55:48,636 --> 00:55:50,513
Julia? - Hi, Mom.

453
00:55:51,639 --> 00:55:53,974
If you get this message, well, you know,

454
00:55:53,975 --> 00:55:55,685
there's so much I wanna say to you.

455
00:55:57,937 --> 00:55:59,438
Happy holidays.

456
00:55:59,439 --> 00:56:02,941
I got you that robot as a present because I've heard

457
00:56:02,942 --> 00:56:05,028
that they're really good companions.

458
00:56:05,945 --> 00:56:09,824
Better than me. I haven't been around for you lately.

459
00:56:11,826 --> 00:56:16,413
Oh, yeah.

460
00:56:16,414 --> 00:56:19,583
I wish I could be there with you right now.

461
00:56:19,584 --> 00:56:21,461
I wish I could just...

462
00:56:23,546 --> 00:56:24,421
Mom?

463
00:57:53,887 --> 00:57:57,765
I'm forever grateful for everything you've done.

464
00:58:00,059 --> 00:58:03,980
I never realised I would miss those moments so much.

465
00:58:06,691 --> 00:58:07,650
I wanna come home.

466
00:58:11,362 --> 00:58:12,280
I love you, mom.



